    {"id":"berlin","title":"Divided Berlin","kind":"TRUCE","phase":"ACTIVE","at":[13.4,52.52],"countries":["USA","RUS","DEU"],"weight":5,"line":{"from":"USA","to":"RUS","style":"rival"},"since":"1958-11","blurb":"Khrushchev's 1958 demand still stands: Western troops out of Berlin, or a separate Soviet treaty with East Germany. Refugees keep crossing west.","sources":["https://history.state.gov/milestones/1961-1968/berlin-crises","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berlin_Crisis_of_1961"]},
    {"id":"algeria","title":"Algerian War","kind":"WAR","phase":"ACTIVE","at":[3,35.6],"countries":["FRA"],"weight":4,"since":"1954-11","blurb":"About 400,000 French troops fight the FLN. De Gaulle has offered self-determination; settlers raise barricades in Algiers on 24 January.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algerian_War","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barricades_Week"]},
    {"id":"cuba","title":"Castro's Cuba","kind":"REGIME","phase":"ACTIVE","at":[-79,21.8],"countries":["CUB","USA"],"weight":4,"line":{"from":"CUB","to":"USA","style":"rival"},"since":"1959-01","blurb":"A year after the revolution, land reform seizes US-owned estates and Havana opens trade talks with Moscow. Washington weighs covert action.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuban_Revolution","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuba%E2%80%93United_States_relations","https://history.state.gov/milestones/1961-1968/bay-of-pigs"]},
    {"id":"korea","title":"Korean armistice line","kind":"TRUCE","phase":"FROZEN","at":[127,38.1],"countries":["KOR","PRK"],"weight":3,"since":"1953-07","blurb":"No peace treaty since the 1953 armistice. Two armies face each other across the DMZ, and Rhee's rule in Seoul is growing brittle.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korean_Armistice_Agreement","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_Revolution"]},
    {"id":"taiwan","title":"Taiwan Strait standoff","kind":"SEA","phase":"FROZEN","at":[118.4,24.45],"countries":["CHN","TWN","USA"],"weight":3,"line":{"from":"CHN","to":"TWN","style":"rival"},"since":"1958-08","blurb":"The 1958 crisis is over, but Chinese batteries still shell Kinmen on odd-numbered days, often with leaflets. The US Seventh Fleet patrols the strait.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Taiwan_Strait_Crisis","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sino-American_Mutual_Defense_Treaty"]},
    {"id":"reggane","title":"A fourth atomic power","kind":"NUCLEAR","phase":"BREWING","at":[0.06,26.3],"countries":["FRA"],"weight":3,"since":"1960-02","blurb":"France's first atomic test, Gerboise Bleue, is set for 13 February near Reggane in the Algerian Sahara.","sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerboise_Bleue","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/France_and_weapons_of_mass_destruction"]},
